Changes: tools/strconv/parse_cases.py selects lines from each file of the
repository's data/ directory (the first lines, evenly spaced lines, the
longest strings, and the subnormal, infinite, and zero results), drops the
float16 field, writes each string's bytes in hexadecimal, and adds the
grammar mode and the acceptance flag.  The other lines of the file, the
decimal inputs of Vern Paxson's tables as reproduced in Go's
src/internal/strconv/testdata/testfp.txt, strings next to midpoints, and
grammar cases, are computed by that program.
